set comments='Officer Abbene Baltimore County Police called After Hours at 12:09am requesting assistance with minor child Dayquan Lee, age 15. Caller stated that police responded to 2920 Liberty Pkwy in reference to a domestic dispute. Upon arrival, they found Dayquan''s mother, Ann Angeles, on the kitchen floor surrounded by blood. Also present was Hysiim Jones (DOB 12/3/97), mother''s boyfriend.

The home belongs to Mr. Jones'' mother, Ms. Tamara Revell (410-918-8033). Ms. Revell reported that she was asleep and heard a commotion which caused her to come out of her room. She then saw Ms. Angeles and Mr. Jones arguing and physically fighting in the kitchen. Mr. Jones allegedly grabbed a knife and stabbed Ms. Angeles in the left arm. Ms. Revell ran out of the home calling for help and a security guard patrolling the area apprehended Mr. Jones until police arrived.

Dayquan was present for the incident. He was transported back to the Dundalk Precinct when officers cleared the scene. Ms. Angeles was transported to JH Bayview for her injuries. Mr. Jones was charged and arrested.

Both Ms. Angeles and Mr. Jones were "high" at the time, under the influence of illicit substances- possibly methamphetamines.

Ms. Angeles has an open warrant in Baltimore County and was apprehended upon her release from the hospital.

Dayquan is diagnosed with ADHD and Autism. He is able to walk but minimally verbal. He says a few words related to food. Dayquan needs assistance with toileting and bathing. He wears a diaper (size M adult depends) and needs to be changed accordingly. Mother states that she is the only one who has ever changed him. Per LE, Tamara Revell advised she is not a resource for Dayquan as she is not a relative of his and cannot care for him.

After Hours worker contacted mother at Bayview who still sounded under the influence. She talked in a low tone with slightly slurred speech. It sounded as if it was difficult for her formulate her thoughts. Ms. Angeles said that she has been staying off/on at 2920 Liberty Pkwy (Ms. Revell’s address). She also said she was "supposed" to be staying in Highlandtown but could not recall where. She then said that she has her own place as of 9/1/19 but could not provide the address. Worker explained that Dayquan was at the Police precinct and we need to find him a place to go. Ms. Angeles advised that she is the only one who cares for him and she has no one else. She advised his father is Donald Lee (DOB of 2/23/73 was located). She advised he lives in the City on Broadway but no further information was provided. She stated there are no relatives or other resources to care for Dayquan. Worker advised that Dayquan would be sheltered to the Department and placed in a foster home.

Worker gathered information about Dayquan for the 872.

After Hours worker made several attempts to locate a placement for Dayquan, exhausting the AH emergency placement list. There were no placements available. AH worker responded to the Dundalk Precinct and sat with Dayquan until the DSS office opened.

